WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.275
The takeaway is simple but powerful.

00:00:02.355 --> 00:00:08.685
You do not need millions of street-view images to
build a state-of-the-art geo-localization model.

00:00:08.765 --> 00:00:11.956
You need the right images and the right knowledge.

00:00:12.036 --> 00:00:17.647
By quantifying which street views are actually
locatable and by borrowing the reasoning

00:00:17.727 --> 00:00:20.198
strategies humans use to win geo-games,

00:00:20.278 --> 00:00:25.431
GeoReasoner matches or beats specialist models with
a fraction of the data, and,

00:00:25.511 --> 00:00:28.047
crucially, it explains every prediction.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:34.850
It is a case study in how data quality and human
inference knowledge can stand in for brute-force scale,

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:40.410
opening a path to geo-localization that is both
interpretable and resource-efficient.
